0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}9-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{9}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3a28deb1-ca63-5cfd-86d0-50d2017028de"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17453e7d-2501-500c-988d-632cc6dfbc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368922} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7fa423-ce11-5e4b-941d-b20daa102519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368923} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf839ad-4dca-5536-a5e6-2102abbf3175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368924} {:answer/id #uuid "d0871187-035d-52b5-b781-f70eaa3bf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} {:answer/id #uuid "0183a8ef-a247-5fec-a72f-23430bb57861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd50738-594a-50f0-9455-2e79aec8430d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "80bd1a5b-eef3-57d3-b7a8-ea1d67708737" :question/math-academy-id "q-95364" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}10-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(10-\\lambda )-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +100-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +64 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -16) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =16,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{16}=4 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4df0b534-5228-58d9-ba3b-1aadcb8d7a6b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552578}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552562 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415548} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415556} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415558} {:answer/id #uuid "c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415563} {:answer/id #uuid "cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/i